A||||10||Wannabe||Tranny Fluid||||1||
Z||000000||Wannabe||05-09-2000||11:43 AM||||Having just made the move from one group of people fanatic about their cars, over to this one, it's surprising the difference in topics of discussion, and this is one that is curiously absent from this group: tranny fluid. One of the first improvements I made to my former "joy ride" was to replace the regular manual tranny fluid with Redline synthetic. There are several different products like this one and they are all designed to improve shifting characteristics and reduce wear. I can honestly say that the stuff works extremely well, smoothing out shifting and elimitating or reducing stickiness when the car is cold. The most popular ones are Redline MTL (synthetic) and  BG Synchroshift (non-synthetic). Apparently there may be some compatability probelms with the synthetic oil and some types of cars, but the BG has no such probelms, so is probably a better choic for the Fiero transmissions. Has anyone here used either of these products in their Fiero?||||reg||1
Z||000001||fieroshop||05-09-2000||11:56 AM||||Wannabe.<BR>I agree with you, all I sell and stock is redline motor oil and also tranny fuid. I have found that redline is more expensive but for my money it is the best.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wannabe||05-09-2000||08:21 PM||||Have you heard of any problems with using Redline MTL in the Fiero tranny?||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||05-09-2000||09:57 PM||||I just did a fluid & filter change on my '88 GT.  I used B&M Trick Shift fluid.  So far so good, but I haven't really driven it yet.  Anyone else have any experience with the B&M fluid?||||reg||14
Z||000004||lowCG||05-10-2000||03:38 AM||||I use the Redline MTL with no problems,shifts great.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Bill Osmer||05-10-2000||10:05 AM||||So if I'm ready to change my "stock" tranny fluid to the Redline MTL, what would be the recommended procedure? If it's in a Haynes or factory service manual, let me know. Specifically, how would you purge ALL of the original fluid before putting new in?||||reg||5
Z||000006||theogre||05-10-2000||10:05 AM||||All brands of Dexron III excede what the TH125c tranny required when it was built.<P>GM documents on Dexron III specify it as being compatible with ALL Dexron using transmissions built since 1940 something.<P>The main dificulty in fluid changes for TH125c is pumping out as much old fluid as posible. In Fiero this should include blowing out the line to the tranny cooler. (those long lines and the cooler hold the better part of a quart.)<P>A new filter and 5-6 quarts of any good brand of Dexron III fluid Will make a diferance in the performance of the tranny. Just how much diferance depends on the condition of the tranny to start with.<P>If you don't get out as much old fluid as psoible, then it really doesn't matter what fluid you put in. You'll still have alot of old fluid and dirt in there, and that will degrade the new fluid significantly.<P>You can never get it all out without pulling the tranny apart or installing a drain in the TC, but you can get most of it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||05-11-2000||10:55 PM||||ive missplaced my notes, can anyone tell em how much fluid i need to put in the getrag.  it was either 2 or 4 quarts, cant remember.||||reg||1
Z||000008||RossT||05-11-2000||11:36 PM||||Its 1.9 quarts||||reg||1
Z||000009||2birds||05-12-2000||09:57 PM||||mrfiero,<BR>A friend of mine just changed over to the B&M Trickshift in his 88 Formula 350 Firebird, and has had no problems.  He also put in a B&M shift kit at the same time, and is very happy with the inprovement.||||reg||1
Z||000010||mrfiero||05-14-2000||12:23 AM||||Thanks 2birds,<P>I don't know if it's just me, but ever since I changed to the Trick Shift fluid my GT pulls all the way to 5500 before shifts (both 1-2 & 2-3).  It just feels better overall.  I had thought about adding a shift kit too, but it looks like I'll have a Northstar in it by next summer, so I probably won't bother.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>   <BR>||||reg||10
